# Run artifacts, regenerated on every pipeline run
# ------------------------------------------------
# These kept turning up as untracked noise in `git status`, which is how a
# real change (a reverted notebook) nearly got committed alongside them.
reports/drift/
reports/hybrid_*.txt
scratch/

# --- Generated output, untracked 2026-08-15 ---------------------------------
# /models/ and __pycache__/ were already listed above, but .gitignore only
# governs UNTRACKED files: these were committed before the rules existed, so
# git kept carrying them. 16,482 Colab batch descriptors and 127 .pyc files
# were dropped from the index (they stay on disk — the training manager and
# the cache scripts still read models/unified locally).
#
# Repeated dumps of one audit: two large JSON files per directory, a dozen
# directories, ~550,000 lines between them.
reports/audit_v1*/
# audit/legacy holds 46 .py files that ARE source; only its output is ignored.
audit/legacy/*.json
audit/legacy/*.html
audit/legacy/*.txt

# The June 2026 audit quarantine: 160 files, 44 MB, referenced by
# src/archive/MANIFEST.md and docs/AUDIT_HISTORY.md as "already-known
# non-live" -- the set they grep to prove code has no live callers. Kept
# locally so those citations point at something; not committed, because no
# code imports it and a fresh clone that lacks it gets the same or a
# stronger answer from the same grep.
/audit/legacy/
